# Trust anchor for Causeway release signatures. See decisions/0019.
#
# tools/verify-release.sh checks a release statement against this file with
# `ssh-keygen -Y verify`. One file of trusted keys, no keyring, no agent, no
# network, no transparency log — which is what lets an egress-restricted
# consumer verify a release at all.
#
# The first column is a principal: a label the verifier prints as the signer.
# It names the release role rather than a person, so rotating the key or the
# maintainer does not change what a consumer trusts.
#
# This file is covered by the bundle digest (tools/build-bundle.sh BUNDLE_FILES)
# and vendored into consuming projects (tools/sync.sh). An anchor a project
# could swap without moving the digest would not be an anchor. Rotating the key
# is therefore a release of the standard, not a settings change.
release@causeway ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIKMCAPc9eWhQbasSdY+kgDldI6g6osDWSVecNHEHsTJo
